# Template. Copy to .env and fill in — .env is gitignored, this file is not.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# These are read by the /decide proxy (server/decide.js, `npm run proxy`), and
# by nothing else. The farm itself still runs entirely in the browser with no
# server and no configuration — the proxy is only needed by animals given a
# ClaudeMind, and ScriptedMind remains the default.
#
# ⚠ NEVER prefix a secret with VITE_.
#   Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the client bundle at build time,
#   so it is shipped to every visitor and readable in devtools. A key belongs
#   in a server process the browser talks to — never in the page itself.
#   Variables without the prefix are not exposed to the client, which is why
#   the ones below have none.

# To use Anthropic directly: fill in ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (get one at https://console.anthropic.com/)
# To use OpenRouter: fill in ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN instead
# If both are set, the gateway wins (cheaper, free models available).

# Anthropic API key (direct). Server-side only.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter gateway (optional). Server-side only.
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Which model that Mind should use.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5

# Port for the proxy that holds the key and serves /decide to the browser.
PORT=8787
